    slug: "network-on-main",
    shortDescription: "Explain exception.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nNetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread. The UI thread should remain responsive, so network I/O belongs in a coroutine, executor, or another appropriate background mechanism. In modern Kotlin code, a common pattern is a suspend API call invoked from a lifecycle-aware scope and moved to Dispatchers.IO when the underlying operation is blocking. AsyncTask is deprecated and should not be recommended for new code.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain the `NetworkOnMainThreadException` accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n2. The UI thread should remain responsive, so network I/O belongs in a coroutine, executor, or another appropriate background mechanism.\n3. In modern Kotlin code, a common pattern is a suspend API call invoked from a lifecycle-aware scope and moved to Dispatchers.IO when the underlying operation is blocking.\n4. Account for lifecycle, configuration changes, process death, and background-execution constraints when the topic touches application state or work..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define it first, explain the part that actually changes the outcome, and use the example to show I understand it in practice.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in an Android application, the behavior can be observed while the app starts, stops, recreates UI state, or processes background work. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn an Android application, this affects runtime behavior, UI state, performance, accessibility, or maintainability depending on the feature. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Ignoring lifecycle changes or process death.\n- Assuming background work can run indefinitely.\n- Updating UI state outside the appropriate lifecycle-aware boundary.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nBring the lifecycle or platform constraint into the answer when relevant. Android behavior often depends on what survives configuration changes and process death.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nNetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread. The UI thread should remain responsive, so network I/O belongs in a coroutine, executor, or another appropriate background mechanism. In modern Kotlin code, a common pattern is a suspend API call invoked from a lifecycle-aware scope and moved to Dispatchers.IO when the underlying operation is blocking. AsyncTask is deprecated and should not be recommended for new code.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain the `NetworkOnMainThreadException` accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n2. The UI thread should remain responsive, so network I/O belongs in a coroutine, executor, or another appropriate background mechanism.\n3. In modern Kotlin code, a common pattern is a suspend API call invoked from a lifecycle-aware scope and moved to Dispatchers.IO when the underlying operation is blocking.\n4. Account for lifecycle, configuration changes, process death, and background-execution constraints when the topic touches application state or work..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define it first, explain the part that actually changes the outcome, and use the example to show I understand it in practice.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in an Android application, the behavior can be observed while the app starts, stops, recreates UI state, or processes background work. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn an Android application, this affects runtime behavior, UI state, performance, accessibility, or maintainability depending on the feature. NetworkOnMainThreadException can occur when an application targeting Honeycomb/API 11 or later performs a network operation on the main thread.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Ignoring lifecycle changes or process death.\n- Assuming background work can run indefinitely.\n- Updating UI state outside the appropriate lifecycle-aware boundary.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nBring the lifecycle or platform constraint into the answer when relevant. Android behavior often depends on what survives configuration changes and process death.",
