    slug: "dispatchers",
    shortDescription: "Explain Dispatchers.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nDispatchers determine the thread(s) used: `Dispatchers.Main` (UI), `Dispatchers.IO` (network/disk), `Dispatchers.Default` (CPU-heavy). Use `withContext()` to switch.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain a `Dispatchers` in coroutines accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Dispatchers determine the thread(s) used: `Dispatchers.Main` (UI), `Dispatchers.IO` (network/disk), `Dispatchers.Default` (CPU-heavy).\n2. Use `withContext()` to switch.\n3. Account for lifecycle, configuration changes, process death, and background-execution constraints when the topic touches application state or work..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with the answer in one sentence, then explain the mechanism that makes it true. Give one concrete example and stop before drifting into unrelated details.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in an Android application, the behavior can be observed while the app starts, stops, recreates UI state, or processes background work. Dispatchers determine the thread(s) used: `Dispatchers.Main` (UI), `Dispatchers.IO` (network/disk), `Dispatchers.Default` (CPU-heavy).\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn an Android application, this affects runtime behavior, UI state, performance, accessibility, or maintainability depending on the feature. Dispatchers determine the thread(s) used: `Dispatchers.Main` (UI), `Dispatchers.IO` (network/disk), `Dispatchers.Default` (CPU-heavy).\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Ignoring lifecycle changes or process death.\n- Assuming background work can run indefinitely.\n- Updating UI state outside the appropriate lifecycle-aware boundary.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nBring the lifecycle or platform constraint into the answer when relevant. Android behavior often depends on what survives configuration changes and process death.",
